  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much each of the five friends will pay if they split the bill equally, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the hamburgers.\n2. Calculate the total cost of the French fries.\n3. Calculate the total cost of the sodas.\n4. Add the cost of the spaghetti.\n5. Sum up all the costs to get the total bill.\n6. Divide the total bill by the number of friends to find out how much each friend will pay.\n\nLet's start with the calculations:\n\n1. The cost of the hamburgers is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ hamburgers} \\times \\$3 \\text{ per hamburger} = \\$15\n   \\]\n\n2. The cost of the French fries is:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ sets of French fries} \\times \\$1.20 \\text{ per set} = \\$4.80\n   \\]\n\n3. The cost of the sodas is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ cups of soda} \\times \\$0.50 \\text{ per cup} = \\$2.50\n   \\]\n\n4. The cost of the spaghetti is:\n   \\[\n   1 \\text{ platter of spaghetti} \\times \\$2.70 \\text{ per platter} = \\$2.70\n   \\]\n\n5. Now, we sum up all the costs to get the total bill:\n   \\[\n   \\$15 + \\$4.80 + \\$2.50 + \\$2.70 = \\$25\n   \\]\n\n6. Finally, we divide the total bill by the number of friends to find out how much each friend will pay:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\$25}{5} = \\$5\n   \\]\n\nSo, each of the five friends will pay \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
